menu "Activity badge"

    choice BADGE_POWER_MODE
        prompt "Sleep strategy between reports"
        default BADGE_POWER_MODE_DEEP_SLEEP
        help
            How the ESP32-H2 sleeps while the LIS2DH12 keeps sampling into its FIFO.

        config BADGE_POWER_MODE_DEEP_SLEEP
            bool "Deep sleep (Zigbee stack restarts and rejoins for every report)"
            help
                Lowest sleep current (about 7 uA for the chip), but every wake-up is a
                full boot and every report a Zigbee rejoin. Each report can pick a nearer
                router again, which suits a wearer who moves around.

        config BADGE_POWER_MODE_LIGHT_SLEEP
            bool "Light sleep (Zigbee stack stays up, no rejoin)"
            help
                About 25 uA sleep current for the chip, but a report is only a short
                radio burst and reading the sensor FIFO needs no boot. Estimated to give
                the longer battery life (see docs/power.md). Requires the console on
                UART0 or disabled.

    endchoice

    config BADGE_REPORT_SAMPLES
        int "Samples per activity report (1 Hz, so seconds)"
        range 10 3600
        default 60
        help
            activity_score is the mean of |a_mag - 1 g| over this many samples.
            60 samples at 1 Hz gives one report per minute.

    config BADGE_BACKOFF_MAX_PERIODS
        int "Longest pause between attempts when the network is unreachable (report periods)"
        range 1 240
        default 16
        help
            After a failed attempt the badge waits 1, 2, 4, ... report periods before
            trying again, up to this limit. Samples keep accumulating meanwhile.

    config BADGE_JOIN_WINDOW_S
        int "Pairing window after power-up or a button press (seconds)"
        range 10 600
        default 180
        help
            How long a factory-new badge keeps looking for a network that permits joining.

    config BADGE_SERVICE_WINDOW_S
        int "Time the badge stays reachable after pairing or a button press (seconds)"
        range 5 300
        default 45
        help
            The badge polls its parent once per second during this window so that
            Zigbee2MQTT can interview and configure it.

    config BADGE_REJOIN_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Time allowed to get back on the network before a report (ms)"
        range 1000 60000
        default 8000

    config BADGE_BATTERY_SENSE
        bool "Measure and report the battery voltage"
        default y
        help
            Disable on a bare devkit without the battery divider.

    config BADGE_BATTERY_REPORT_PERIOD
        int "Report the battery every N activity reports"
        depends on BADGE_BATTERY_SENSE
        range 1 1440
        default 10

    config BADGE_ZB_CHANNEL_MASK
        hex "Zigbee channels scanned first when pairing"
        range 0x800 0x07FFF800
        default 0x07FFF800
        help
            Bit n = channel n (11..26). Set only the channel of your Zigbee2MQTT
            network (e.g. 0x800 for channel 11) to make pairing faster and cheaper.

    config BADGE_ZB_TX_POWER_DBM
        int "Zigbee transmit power (dBm)"
        range -24 20
        default 10
        help
            TX current is about 36 mA at 0 dBm, 60 mA at 9 dBm and 140 mA at 20 dBm.

    config BADGE_ZB_POLL_INTERVAL_S
        int "Parent poll interval while idle (seconds)"
        range 1 900
        default 300
        help
            Only matters in light-sleep mode, where the stack stays up between
            reports. Must stay well below the 64-minute end-device timeout.

    config BADGE_ZB_MANUFACTURER
        string "Zigbee manufacturer name (Basic cluster)"
        default "ActivityBadge"

    config BADGE_ZB_MODEL
        string "Zigbee model identifier (Basic cluster)"
        default "AB-H2-LIS2DH12"
        help
            Zigbee2MQTT selects the converter by this string (zigbeeModel).

endmenu
